<title>USA: Waigel - conditions good for growth in world trade.</title>
<headline>Waigel - conditions good for growth in world trade.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel said on Sunday that conditions were good for growth in world trade.</p>
<p>In a speech to the interim committee of the International Monetary Fund, Waigel said, &quot;The framework conditions for a continuation in the expansion of world trade are favourable.&quot;</p>
<p>Waigel said that the overall prospects for the world economy had improved since the Interim Committee last met in April. &quot;The growth rates in the world economy will grow. The volume of world trade is growing at a proportionately faster rate.&quot; he added.</p>
<p>--Washington Newsroom +1 202 898 8300</p>
</text>
